cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MIPLIB-Infeas: Primal- and Dual-Infeasible Linear Programs from MIPLIB 2017"
message: >-
  If you use this collection, please cite it as below. MIPLIB 2017 should be cited
  alongside it: every instance here is derived from one of theirs.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Lu
    given-names: Haihao
    affiliation: Massachusetts Institute of Technology
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Bo
    affiliation: Massachusetts Institute of Technology
abstract: >-
  334 linear programs with no optimal solution, each derived from a MIPLIB 2017
  instance with its integrality dropped. 229 have no feasible point: each is a node
  a branch-and-bound search reached and pruned. The other 105 are feasible with an
  unbounded objective, produced by removing a minimal set of bounds and constraints
  from a root relaxation. They run up to 20,682,487 variables and 19,912,111
  constraints, and are intended as a benchmark for infeasibility and unboundedness
  detection.
keywords:
  - linear programming
  - infeasibility detection
  - unbounded linear programs
  - benchmark
  - MIPLIB
  - mathematical optimization
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/MIT-Lu-Lab/MIPLIB-Infeas"
url: "https://mit-lu-lab.github.io/MIPLIB-Infeas"
year: 2026
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "MIPLIB 2017: Data-Driven Compilation of the 6th Mixed-Integer Programming Library"
    url: "https://miplib.zib.de/"
    year: 2021
    authors:
      - name: The MIPLIB 2017 team
